title: Authorizations › Reviews this week › After a review is signed
route: /authorizations?view=reviews
intro: What the demo does once a clinician signs. The review changes status, its row changes, and Cadence books the next review: the review's own date plus the interval. When the next review falls before the end of Sunday it takes the signed one's place on the row; otherwise the row stays 'Signed' and the drawer says when the next one is.
dir: TD
also: The PRD (03, Prior Authorization Lifecycle) treats each signed request as a version that is kept, and times renewals from the binding date and the payer's lead time. The demo books the next review from the interval alone and does not send the signed review anywhere.
---
start s1 "A clinician signature is saved\n(one review, or 'Sign all clean drafts')"
store st1 "The review keeps: status 'Signed', who signed, the demo-clock time, and the draft text as signed"

group gScreen "What changes on screen"
  process a1 "Row: 'Review' reads 'Signed'; 'Check to look at' goes\nThe button is the row's own again: 'Open', 'Send to payer', 'Open on Dashboard'"
  process a2 "Drawer, if open: footer reads 'Signed by Heather K., LISW-S', the draft is read-only, and a green banner shows 'Next review: Tue 10/27, 9:00 am'"
  process a3 "Reviews this week still counts the row: 47 stays 47"
  process a5 "'Sign all clean drafts' is greyed out once none are left on screen"
  process a7 "The sidebar badge does not change\nA tracked case with nothing else open leaves 'Needs attention'"
endgroup

group gNext "The next review"
  agent g1 "Cadence books the next continued-stay review\nDate: the review's own date and time plus the interval (from now, if it was signed late)"
  process i1 "Interval: the payer's own rule when Payers has one ('A continued-stay review every 7 days'), else the level of care\nResidential and PHP 7 days, IOP 14 days, Detox 3 days. The sooner of the two wins"
  store n1 "A new review is saved: next review number (e.g. review 3), same time of day, status 'Not drafted yet'\nThe signed review remembers the date"
  toast t1 "Toast: 'R-0856 was signed by Heather K., LISW-S. Cadence booked the next review for Tue 10/27, 9:00 am.'\n('Sign all clean drafts': 'Cadence booked the next review for each.')"
  decision d1 "Does the next review fall before the end of Sunday?"
  process n2 "It takes the row's place on this week's list, as 'Not drafted yet' with 'Open the review'\n'Draft all due reviews' drafts it (Detox reviews do: every 3 days)"
  process n3 "The row stays 'Signed'\nThe drawer says 'It falls after this week, so it is not on the list yet.'"
  process n4 "A ledger row's Deadline reads 'Next review Tue 10/27', then 'Review due' when the day comes\nThe ledger status goes to 'On track', so 'Needs action' and 'Review due' leave the row\n'Runs out before review' may now show (R-0856, I-2193)"
  process n5 "Ledger case page: a 'Next review' line and, in the history, 'Cadence booked review 3'"
  ext x1 "Payer receives the signed review through its portal or by fax (real product, not drawn in the demo)"
endgroup

group gCase "Case record"
  click c1 "Click 'Open case' in the drawer"
  goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Draft › Read and edit"
  goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Ledger case page › Open and read"
endgroup
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › Approved › Units used and the run-out flag"

store st2 "'Reset demo data' puts every review back to its starting state, clears signatures and removes the booked reviews"
end e1 "Review is signed and counted"

s1 --> st1
st1 --> a1 & a2 & a3 & a5 & a7
st1 --> g1 --> i1 --> n1 --> t1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| n2
d1 -->|No| n3
n2 --> n4
n3 --> n4
n4 --> n5
n4 -.-> g4
n1 -.-> x1
a2 --> c1 --> g2
c1 -.-> g3
a1 & a3 & a5 & a7 --> e1
n5 --> e1
e1 -.-> st2
